## Pattern 2: Two Pointers

The **Two Pointers** technique reduces brute-force nested loops into a **single linear scan**.

### Core Idea
- Use two indices moving strategically
- Either move towards each other or in the same direction

### Common Use Cases
- Two Sum in sorted arrays  
- Palindrome validation  
- Removing duplicates in-place  
- Array merging  

**Time Complexity:** O(n)  
**Space Complexity:** O(1)

![Two Pointers](/images/blogs/mastering-dsa-patterns/two-pointers.png)

