## Pattern 4: Prefix Sum

Prefix Sum enables **instant range queries** after preprocessing.

### Core Formula (Text Only)
The sum of elements from index i to j can be calculated as:  
sum(i, j) = prefix[j] − prefix[i − 1]

### Best Use Cases
- Subarray sum problems
- Range queries
- 2D matrix sums

### Popular Problems
- Subarray Sum Equals K  
- Product of Array Except Self  
- Range Sum Query  

![Prefix Sum](/images/blogs/mastering-dsa-patterns/prefix-sum.png)

