## Pattern 6: DFS and BFS

These traversal techniques are essential for trees, graphs, and grids.

### DFS (Depth-First Search)
- Explores deeply before backtracking
- Uses recursion or stack
- Best for pathfinding and cycle detection

### BFS (Breadth-First Search)
- Explores level by level
- Uses a queue
- Best for shortest path problems

![DFS BFS](/images/blogs/mastering-dsa-patterns/dfs-bfs.png)

---

## Pattern 7: Backtracking and Dynamic Programming

### Backtracking
- Explore all possibilities
- Prune invalid paths early
- Used in permutations, N-Queens, Sudoku

### Dynamic Programming
- Break problems into subproblems
- Store results to avoid recomputation
- Converts exponential time into polynomial time

![Backtracking DP](/images/blogs/mastering-dsa-patterns/backtracking-dp.png)

